WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.697
Anthony Peeples: We have between 800

00:00:03.697 --> 00:00:05.940
and 1,000 Funko Pops, give or take.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.200
I'm Anthony Peeples.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.810
I'm a Funko Pop Collector.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:10.440
I'm feeling high-five fantastic,

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.940
and I hope you are as well.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.500
Narrator: Funko Pops are everywhere.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.510
They're those small plastic figurines

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.260
with giant heads and big round eyes.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.420
There are pops of pretty much

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.140
every character you can think of.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.302
And fans are obsessed.

00:00:24.302 --> 00:00:26.810
The company did half a billion dollars

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.920
in sales in 2017.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.910
And has already surpassed that in 2018.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.530
Anthony, who goes by the
nickname GeekyPeeples,

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:38.250
has taken his obsession to another level.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.340
Peeples: Funko Funatics is
definitely a common term

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.200
that we all use to refer to ourselves.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.750
Narrator: Anthony and his partner, Raul,

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.950
have been collecting Pops since 2015.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.320
And they can be found all over their home.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.950
Peeples: They're displayed
in all the various places

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.109
that we can find room in our

00:00:55.109 --> 00:00:56.890
New York City apartment.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.180
We have one room that is our room that

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.490
we've kind of transformed into a Pop den.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:07.460
My DC wall is dedicated to
"Batman the Animated Series,"

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.110
which was very important to me

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.180
in my childhood growing up.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.320
I'm a big Marvel boy,

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:15.060
so I collect a lot of the Marvel lines.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.423
I have one wall dedicated to Freddy Funko,

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:19.930
the Funko mascot.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.927
The other wall is kind of,

00:01:22.927 --> 00:01:24.220
"storage."

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.180
It's a slow process so
I'm building the room up.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.490
Narrator: His kitchen is decorated

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.360
with Pops that are food related.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.030
Peeples: A friend of mine,
he actually displays his

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.320
Mr. Freeze Pops in the freezer.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.100
Narrator: And when we visited in October,

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.040
his living room was decorated
with Halloween-related Pops.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.220
Peeples: So all of the
Pops that are horror based,

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:44.780
or fun, or scary.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.270
And we also have Pops
displayed in our bedroom.

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:48.730
Narrator: Anthony keeps track of his Pops

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.610
using several online apps.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.300
Which estimate that his collection

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.500
could be worth thousands of dollars,

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.333
based on market value.

00:01:56.325 --> 00:01:58.900
But the prices can change over time.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.400
His first Pop was a Storm figurine

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.630
given to him as a gift from friends.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:05.463
Peeples: And then from there,

00:02:05.463 --> 00:02:08.463
it just took fire in side of me

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.700
and I just wanted to
collect as many as I can.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.130
I actually still have that Storm,

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:13.750
it's right there on the wall.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.990
I keep it right where I can always see it.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.050
Narrator: His collection
includes many rare Pops

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.380
that were released as limited editions.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:22.070
Including some ultra rare ones

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.950
called Chase Pops.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:28.950
Peeples: A Chase Pop is
a Pop that you can find,

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.160
kind of like the golden ticket

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.070
that Willy Wonka was giving out.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.610
It's very rare, and there's only

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.100
a certain limited amount of them.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.060
And they also have a
special sticker on them.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.350
Also, if you collect comics,

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.910
it's like a variant cover.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.210
Narrator: In 2017, he
went to the grand opening

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:46.490
of the Funko Headquarters in Washington.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:49.400
And got his hands on one of
his most prized figurines.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:50.570
Peeples: It's the Emerald Freddy.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.090
It has the flagship sticker on it,

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:53.370
which was also very rare.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.230
I also have another very rare Pop.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.730
The blue chrome Batman

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.630
from San Diego Comic Con.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.230
I slept for four days

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:04.870
in front of the San Diego Convention,

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.870
and I ended up getting into the booth.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.440
I cried a lot because I was so happy

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:09.930
and so excited.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:13.340
The chrome Batman is worth a lot of money.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.930
I've seen it go up right now, currently,

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:17.970
as high on Ebay as $800.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:19.430
Narrator: He and his partner also placed

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:22.400
in a lipsyncing contest at a Funko Event.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.830
And chose two giant Robin
and Joker Pops as prizes,

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.910
that he estimates are now
worth about $1,200 each.

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:33.550
Peeples: I do also have just
a couple rare Proto Pops.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:34.383
Narrator: These are basically

00:03:34.383 --> 00:03:37.850
prototypes of Pops before
they're massed produced.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.039
Anthony doesn't just
collect Pops, however,

00:03:40.039 --> 00:03:43.140
he also organizes events
with fellow collectors,

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.654
including fundraisers for charity.

00:03:45.654 --> 00:03:49.809
Peeples: I host here in
New York, periodically,

00:03:49.809 --> 00:03:52.860
events that I call Peeples Pop!Swap.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:55.140
Those events have been
major, major moments

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:58.750
where I've gotten to
meet so many collectors

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:00.700
and have so many wonderful friends

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:01.960
because of that.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.500
Narrator: In addition to swapping,

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.240
Anthony often sells Pops
to help fund his trips

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:09.820
to various conventions around
the world to buy new ones.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.220
Peeples: Cause it's very expensive.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:15.200
The expenses do mount up.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.980
Narrator: He's active in
the official Funko Forum,

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.660
a message board for fans.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:21.350
So he always knows where to be

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.470
to get the rare Pops for cheap.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:26.000
Peeples: I try to get them as close to

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.418
the retail value that they come out for.

00:04:28.418 --> 00:04:29.720
Narrator: But he will occasionally

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.240
have to pay upwards of $100 for some

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.570
that he missed to complete his set.

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.628
He has a few basic tips for Funko hunters.

00:04:37.628 --> 00:04:39.830
Peeples: So it's best
to just be on your game.

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.460
Know your information.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.360
Know where the Pop is you want.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:46.220
Know how much it's going to cost.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.330
And be prepared to line up

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.980
and hopefully score some
wonderful Funko Pops.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.480
Narrator: And he says he has no desire

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:56.130
to stop collecting anytime soon.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.720
Peeples: Whether I
collect Funko Pops or not,

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.760
the one thing that is a constant,

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.320
is that the people I've met

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.920
and the relationships I've established

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.130
from being in the Funko Pop community,

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.030
they're not going anywhere in my heart.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:09.397
I will keep in contact whether
I collect Funkos or not.

00:05:09.397 --> 00:05:11.250
And there's a story behind each one.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.540
Some people identify
themselves as "I'm a fiend!"

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.070
and they'll be wearing the fiend patch.

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:16.140
Or they're a Funkero.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:19.140
There's Jersey Funko and
there's Chicago Funko.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:21.300
So many across the country

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.830
and they identify themselves in that way.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.400
But we're all Funatics,

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.650
we're all Funko Funatics.

